<title>BELGIUM: Solvay buys Nokia's 25% of Finnper.</title>
<headline>Solvay buys Nokia's 25% of Finnper.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian chemicals group Solvay said on Friday it increased its stake in Finnish chemicals group Oy Finnish Peroxides AB (Finnper) to 75 percent from 50 percent by acquiring the interest of the Nokia Group.  </p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The remaining 25 percent of Finnper remains in the hands of Finnish paper group UPM-Kymmene, Solvay said.</p>
<p>Finnper makes hydrogen peroxide, a bleaching agent used in, among others, the paper industry.</p>
<p>&quot;This move strengthens the position of Solvay in the Nordic countries and reflects Solvay's strategy of developing its position as a leading supplier of the pulp and paper industry,&quot; Solvay said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Scandinavian pulp industry consumes more than half the total European output of hydrogen peroxide, Solvay noted.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
